 <body> 
  <code><script type="text/javascript"></script> 
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="techdocs_85_11_word.css"/> 
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="/etc/designs/cdc/transformation/techdocs_85_11_word.css"/></code> 
  <div class="WordSection1"> 
   <p class="pBody">&nbsp;</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068726">Executive summary</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Security fused into the network.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Enterprise networks are undergoing a fundamental transformation. Organizations must securely connect an expanding ecosystem of users, devices, applications, cloud services, AI-driven workloads, and autonomous agents while maintaining operational simplicity, resilience, and security. Hybrid workforces, distributed campuses and branches, cloud-native applications, operational technology, IoT devices, and emerging AI services have dramatically increased the scale and complexity of modern environments.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">At the same time, the threat landscape continues to evolve. AI-powered attacks now operate at machine speed, data exfiltration remains a top business risk, and traditional perimeter-focused security models are no longer sufficient. Organizations must not only secure external access points but also continuously authenticate users, devices, and agents, enforce least-privilege access, contain lateral movement, and maintain visibility across increasingly dynamic environments.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">These challenges require a new approach where networking and security operate as a unified system rather than separate technology domains. Cisco Secure Networking (CSN) fuses security into the fabric of the enterprise network, making the network an ever-present security layer that protects customer data, financial systems, business continuity, regulatory compliance, and digital experiences wherever the business runs. As the traditional perimeter dissolves, fragmented, bolt-on security cannot keep pace with machine-speed exploitation, AI-driven lateral movement, infrastructure-targeted attacks, compromised identities, and the “harvest-now, decrypt-later” quantum threat. </p> 
   <p class="pBody">By strengthening infrastructure resilience, establishing common policy context through Cisco Data Fabric, and using unified management and agentic operations, CSN gives networking and security teams a connected foundation for protecting infrastructure, traffic, workloads, people, AI agents, and digital experiences.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068727">Delivering value via three key pillars</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">As enterprise environments continue to evolve, the network must deliver three connected outcomes. First, organizations need a trusted, resilient infrastructure. Second, the network must protect every flow. Finally, Unified Management and Agentic Operations must bring these capabilities together through assurance, automation, and action for people and AI agents.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Cisco Secure Networking delivers these outcomes through three pillars: </p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Trust the Infrastructure</b>: Cisco strengthens infrastructure resilience across campus, branch, WAN, remote access, cloud, and workload environments. This secure infrastructure connects what is allowed, enforces policy, and provides the telemetry and common policy context needed for distributed enforcement and assurance.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt;font-weight:normal"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Establish Device Trust by verifying every platform from power-on through runtime using technologies such as secure boot, hardened operating system implementations, image signing, runtime integrity monitoring, and Cisco Live Protect.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Act as the intelligent foundation for connectivity, distributed policy enforcement, and telemetry, enabling operational services and a common policy context.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt;font-weight:normal"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Prove trust through modern advanced crypto agility with technologies such as MACsec, post-quantum readiness, and continuous compliance evidence.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Secure Every Flow</b>: The network must protect every interaction across users, devices, workloads, applications, and AI agents. This involves securing all steps across the infrastructure from entry through application and data access. Cisco Data Fabric carries the data, telemetry, and context required to apply policy consistently across domains, while distributed enforcement capabilities enact those policies. Threat intelligence and analytics then enable detection and response at machine speed to reduce threat impact and accelerate recovery.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Cisco Secure Networking protects every flow through four connected functions:</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><b>Secure Infrastructure</b>: The trusted, resilient foundation consisting of the physical topology, routed Layer 3 underlay, OSPF transport, device reachability, MTU consistency, redundancy, and foundational telemetry.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><b>Identify and Authorize:</b> Identity- and context-aware access control using Cisco ISE, 802.1X, MAB, endpoint profiling, authorization profiles, and Security Group Tag assignment.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><b>Segment and Protect:</b> Least-privilege reachability control using VLANs, VRFs, VXLAN EVPN, SGTs, TrustSec, Adaptive Policy, SD-WAN segmentation, and distributed firewall enforcement.</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><b>Detect and Respond:</b> Detection, correlation, and governed containment using network telemetry, encrypted traffic analytics, firewall inspection, threat intelligence, XDR, and distributed response actions.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Assure Every Experience</b>: Unified Management and Agentic Operations, delivered through Cisco Cloud Control, unify the platform through one operating model. Assurance, automation, and governed action help networking and security teams preserve availability, performance, and the digital experience while maintaining human control.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Cisco Cloud Control brings these capabilities together through:</p> 
   <p class="pBody" style="margin-top:0in;margin-right:.3in;margin-bottom:3.0pt;margin-left:.5in;text-indent:-.25in"><span style="font-family:Symbol">&middot;<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Centralized Management connects inventory, topology, health, assurance, security, and operational context through Cisco Cloud Control and Cisco Data Fabric.</p> 
   <p class="pBody" style="margin-top:0in;margin-right:.3in;margin-bottom:3.0pt;margin-left:.5in;text-indent:-.25in"><span style="font-family:Symbol">&middot;<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Agentic Operations turn shared context and operational insight into governed action at machine speed while maintaining human control.</p> 
   <p class="pBody" style="margin-top:0in;margin-right:.3in;margin-bottom:3.0pt;margin-left:.5in;text-indent:-.25in"><span style="font-family:Symbol">&middot;<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Continuous Assurance by verifying security, availability, performance, and policy outcomes end to end.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Together, these pillars address the three pressures above. The next section explains why they must work as one architecture.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068728">Challenge statement</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Why now? Threats and operations move at machine speed.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">The enterprise attack surface is evolving faster than legacy security models can respond. AI-accelerated exploitation is shrinking vulnerability-remediation windows and increasing the risk to network devices and control planes, while “harvest-now, decrypt-later” attacks threaten long-lived data and expose the lack of crypto agility in existing infrastructure. At the same time, AI agents are emerging as high-privilege identities whose access, traffic, and behavior can be difficult to discover and govern, creating new paths for lateral movement. Fragmented tools, overlapping policies, and limited end-to-end visibility prevent NetOps and SecOps from acting quickly without disrupting connectivity or the digital experience. Organizations need a more integrated approach that can keep infrastructure resilient, govern every identity, protect every flow, and assure every experience. </p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068729">Three pressures expose legacy security limits</a></p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">1.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Infrastructure risk is outpacing traditional protection.</span> AI can compress vulnerability-remediation windows, target network devices and control planes, and increase exposure before teams can patch. Long-lived data also faces harvest-now, decrypt-later risk when infrastructure lacks crypto agility.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">2.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Every new identity expands the attack surface.</span> AI agents can hold credentials, access sensitive applications and data, and generate traffic that existing tools cannot always discover or govern. They must be identified, continuously verified, governed, and contained with the same rigor applied to human and machine identities.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">3.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Visibility gaps put every experience at risk.</span> Fragmented NetOps and SecOps tools, overlapping policies, and limited end-to-end visibility make it difficult to understand policy impact or act quickly without disrupting legitimate traffic and the digital experience.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><span class="BodyBold"><span style="font-weight:normal">The three pillars of Cisco Secure Networking provide a structured response to these press</span></span>ures.</p> 
   <div> 
    <table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="100%" bordercolor="#ADADAD"> 
     <thead> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Pillar</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Primary technical mechanism</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Result</span></p> </td> 
      </tr> 
     </thead> 
     <tbody> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Trust the Infrastructure</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Operate hardened devices and a resilient, intelligent infrastructure that provides secure connectivity, distributed policy enforcement, and telemetry to assure the experience.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">A trusted, resilient, verifiable foundation for secure access, distributed enforcement, telemetry, and recovery.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Secure Every Flow</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Apply the four connected functions—identify and authorize; segment and protect; detect; and respond—to users, devices, workloads, and agents wherever traffic moves.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Least-privilege access, distributed protection, reduced threat impact, and faster recovery wherever traffic moves.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Assure Every Experience</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Unify operations through Cisco Cloud Control, centralized management, governed agentic operations, and continuous assurance.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">One operating model that helps networking and security teams act from shared context across every experience</p> </td> 
