   </div> 
   <p class="pBody">&nbsp;</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068730">Why fragmented controls reach a limit</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Point products remain viable within their domains, but enterprise outcomes depend on how identity, policy, detection, response, and assurance connect across domains; whether identity context reaches enforcement, segmentation follows identity rather than topology, detection triggers coordinated responses, and assurance verifies that the resulting action protects both security and user experience. A collection of controls is not yet an architecture.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068731">Desired customer outcomes</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Start with the business result.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Executives and business buyers enter the secure networking conversation through outcomes such as simplification, resilience, secure access, risk reduction, and secure agentic AI. These outcomes provide a common lens for security, networking, infrastructure, risk, and finance leaders to evaluate one connected architecture.</p> 
