   <p class="pBody">&nbsp;</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="672" height="107" id="Picture 15" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_5.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068736">Cisco products in the framework</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Cisco portfolio products serve the framework, not vice versa.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Cisco combines networking, identity, security, observability, and threat intelligence so controls can share context and enforce policy where traffic is created and consumed. Product choice remains deployment-specific; the framework provides the stable design logic.</p> 
   <div> 
    <table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="100%" bordercolor="#ADADAD"> 
     <thead> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Framework capability</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Cisco portfolio examples</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="Cellhead1"><span style="color:white">Architectural value</span></p> </td> 
      </tr> 
     </thead> 
     <tbody> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Secure Infrastructure</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Catalyst switching and wireless; Cisco Secure Routers and SD-WAN; industrial platforms; Trust Anchor, SUDI, Secure Boot, signed images, runtime integrity; Cisco Live Protect; Splunk Exposure Analytics; MACsec and IPsec.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">A trusted, resilient, verifiable foundation for distributed enforcement, telemetry, and recovery</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Identify and Authorize</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Cisco ISE; Access Manager; Duo; Identity Intelligence; Secure Access; Secure Client; Cyber Vision; Secure Workload discovery.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Discover and classify identities and assets, evaluate context, and make continuous least-privilege access decisions.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Segment and Protect</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Software-Defined Access; TrustSec and Security Group Tags; Meraki Adaptive Policy; Secure Workload; Isovalent; Secure Firewall; Hybrid Mesh Firewall.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Express business intent once, reduce attack paths, and enforce closer to users, devices, workloads, and resources.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Detect</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Secure Firewall; Encrypted Traffic Analytics and Encrypted Visibility Engine; Secure Network Analytics; Secure Access DNS; Multicloud Defense; AI Defense; Cisco Talos.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Combine pervasive telemetry, behavior analytics, inspection, and threat intelligence to find abnormal activity across encrypted and distributed environments.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Respond</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Cisco XDR; Splunk SOAR; ISE Rapid Threat Containment and Adaptive Network Control; Secure Endpoint; Security in Cloud Control; distributed network and security enforcement.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Correlate evidence and contain the affected identity, endpoint, segment, workload, or flow with governed and reversible action.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Common Policy Context</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Cisco Data Fabric; Cisco ISE; Access Manager; Duo; Secure Client; Secure Workload; Security Group Tags.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Carry identity, posture, role, workload, application, and risk context across policy and enforcement domains.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Unified Management and Agentic Operations</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Cisco Cloud Control; Splunk; Catalyst Center; Meraki Dashboard; Nexus Dashboard; SD-WAN Manager; Secure Firewall Management Center; AI Canvas; Cisco AI Assistant; Deep Network Model; Splunk Agentic SOC; Splunk AI Assistant; ThousandEyes; Catalyst Center Assurance; Meraki Health; SD-WAN analytics; Splunk observability and security telemetry.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Connects inventory, topology, health, assurance, security, and operational context. Supports investigation and bounded action, with guardrails, auditability, approvals, rollback, and human control. Verifies security efficacy, reachability, path health, policy outcomes, performance, and digital experience across owned and unowned infrastructure.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr valign="top" align="left"> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none"><span class="BodyBold">Extended Integrations</span></p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">ServiceNow and other ITSM/CMDB systems; third-party SIEM/SOC platforms and firewalls; identity providers; public clouds; documented APIs; infrastructure-as-code workflows; collaboration, IoT, and AI data center ecosystems.</p> </td> 
       <td> <p class="pChart_bodyCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-left: 3pt; margin-right: 3pt; margin-top: 3pt; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0pt; text-transform: none">Connects secure networking with the customer’s operating model while sharing policy, telemetry, and automation across domains.</p> </td> 
      </tr> 
     </tbody> 
    </table> 
   </div> 
   <p class="pBody">Portfolio names and packaging evolve. Architecture decisions should be validated against current release, licensing, interoperability, and lifecycle guidance.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="671" height="107" id="Picture 16" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_6.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068737">Lab testing validation and proof</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>Evidence with clear boundaries.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Using the framework as a model, teams built a Cisco Secure Network in the lab with the goal of testing to the stated business outcomes and objectives.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068738">What was tested</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Validation procedures examined the Secure Network Reference Architecture as an integrated system rather than as a collection of isolated features. Across campus, branch, and distributed deployment models, the scope included:</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Resilient connectivity, routing, availability, and failover</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Scalable macrosegmentation and microsegmentation</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Identity-driven access, authorization, and posture validation</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Application, remote access, WAN, and cloud connectivity</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Policy enforcement across network and security domains</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Telemetry, observability, centralized management, and assurance</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Operational workflows, including onboarding, policy changes, and service disruptions</p> 
   <p class="pBulletCMT" style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal;margin-bottom: 3pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none"><span style="font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;position:relative;top:-.5pt"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Integrations with security, analytics, observability, and IT service-management platforms</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Testing considered both steady-state operations and dynamic or degraded conditions to assess end-to-end architectural behavior.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">The reference architecture establishes validated design intent; deployment guides translate that intent into implementation guidance for specific deployment scenarios.</p> 
   <div class=" pDefault">
     Figure 3. Architecture-to-deployment guide handoff 
   </div> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="695" height="210" id="Picture 26" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_7.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068739">What validation demonstrated</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Validation demonstrates that the Secure Network Reference Architecture can deliver consistent operational and security outcomes across its architecture domains when deployed according to validated design guidance. The architecture supports resilient connectivity, scalable segmentation, identity-driven policy enforcement, and consistent access across wired, wireless, remote access, and application environments.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Unified Management and Agentic Operations provide lifecycle management, shared telemetry, policy orchestration, and operational assurance. Extended Integrations connect security, analytics, observability, and IT service-management platforms to support coordinated workflows and improved operational response.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Together, these capabilities support scalable growth, resilient operations, predictable performance, consistent policy enforcement, and operational efficiency across supported deployment models.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068740">A proof-of-value method</a></p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">1.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Baseline the current state, including operational effort, exposure, reachability, detection and containment time, application experience, and change failure rate.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">2.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Select one high-value outcome and design representative normal, degraded, and adversarial scenarios.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">3.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Execute using the intended deployment model, identity sources, traffic paths, policy, and integrations.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">4.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Observe whether context is correlated across identity, network, security, and experience telemetry.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">5.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Contain through the intended enforcement point and verify that essential service remains available.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">6.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Recover or roll back, document evidence, and compare results with the baseline before scaling.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068741">Representative scenarios</a></p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">1.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>A compromised valid identity attempts lateral movement.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">2.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>An unmanaged or industrial device initiates prohibited communications.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">3.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Suspicious behavior is hidden inside encrypted traffic.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">4.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>A critical infrastructure exposure must be mitigated before a patch window.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">5.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><b>Secure agentic AI:</b> An AI agent with valid credentials attempts to invoke an unapproved tool or access data outside its task scope. Identify the agent and owner, apply least privilege, inspect agent-to-tool traffic, detect abnormal behavior, and require bounded, auditable action with human control.</p> 
   <div class=" pDefault">
     Figure 4. Secure agentic AI use case workflow 
   </div> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="696" height="177" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_8.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068742">Implement framework incrementally</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>A practical operating model.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Secure networking does not require a single cutover or a universal management plane. The framework can guide staged modernization around the customer’s highest-risk flows and most valuable outcomes. The platform approach represents the target state; the sequence below provides early evidence while building reusable identity, policy, telemetry, and automation foundations.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068743">1. Align on outcomes and ownership</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Bring NetOps, SecOps, identity, cloud, application, industrial, and service-management leaders into one decision model. Define the first outcome, the accountable owner, the risk boundary, and the measures that will determine success.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068744">2. Establish trusted context</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Inventory critical infrastructure and flows. Improve identity and asset discovery. Normalize role, posture, workload, and application context. Identify where policy translations or stale privileges create avoidable exposure.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068745">3. Reduce reachability and improve detection</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Apply segmentation to a bounded use case, add telemetry at the relevant paths, and connect detection to response. Favor controls that preserve business communication while removing unnecessary paths.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068746">4. Automate with governance</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Automate stable, repeatable actions first. Define approval thresholds, service-impact guardrails, logging, exception handling, and rollback before expanding to agentic workflows or higher-impact change.</p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068747">5. Assure, learn, and scale</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Verify user and application experience after every control change. Use evidence from incidents, policy exceptions, and proof-of-value testing to refine the architecture and prioritize the next domain.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="671" height="107" id="Picture 18" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_9.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead1"><a name="_Toc243068748">Summary: Why Cisco</a></p> 
   <p class="pBody"><b>One architecture across network, security, and experience.</b></p> 
   <p class="pBody">Secure networking is needed because enterprise risk now travels through the same distributed relationships that deliver the business. Users, devices, workloads, applications, APIs, and AI agents must communicate across infrastructure the enterprise does not fully own. Protecting those interactions requires more than visibility and more than a collection of perimeter controls. It requires a trusted, identity-aware, distributed, closed-loop architecture. </p> 
   <p class="pToC_Subhead2"><a name="_Toc243068749">Cisco’s differentiated value</a></p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">1.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">The network becomes an enforcement fabric.</span> Cisco can apply identity-aware policy close to users, devices, workloads, and resources across campus, branch, data center, cloud, and remote access.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">2.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Security and networking share context.</span> Identity, policy, telemetry, threat intelligence, and experience data can inform the same control loop instead of remaining trapped in separate operational domains.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">3.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Trust begins below the policy layer.</span> Hardware and software integrity, runtime protection, encryption, exposure prioritization, and cryptographic readiness protect the infrastructure that carries and enforces intent.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">4.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Response is distributed and experience-aware.</span> Controls can contain closer to the affected flow while assurance verifies that essential service and digital experience remain intact.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">5.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">Governed Agentic Operations turns connected context into action.</span> AI-assisted investigation and bounded automation can accelerate response while guardrails, auditability, approvals, rollback, and organizational policy keep people in control.</p> 
   <p class="pStep1CMT">6.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span class="BodyBold">The architecture accommodates choice and staged adoption.</span> Open integrations and multiple deployment models let customers extend current investments while converging on shared functions and measurable outcomes.</p> 
   <p class="pBody">Cloud Control unifies the operating model, Data Fabric provides shared context, and resilient infrastructure provides the foundation for protecting flows and experiences.</p> 
   <p class="pBody"><img width="695" height="111" id="Picture 19" src="/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/solutions/CVD/Campus/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture.docx/_jcr_content/renditions/Intro-Cisco-Secure-Network-Architecture_10.jpg" alt="Related image, diagram or screenshot"/></p> 
  </div>  
 </body>
</html>

    
    













